: the bug was in chipset which perevents of using some new 64bit PCI devices
: only. 32bit PCI is clean.

Old PWS system boads (pre-April'97, if I remember right) have a PCI 
chipset bug which would cause silent data corruption under high load,
when multiple PCI cards are present. E.g., it would _occationally_ result
in corruped data in configurations with two SCSI controllers - this was
the reason why older PWS systems do not support external SCSI devices.
For all I know, they may also have problems with 64-bit PCI cards - but
since I never used any of those in PWS, I wasn't paying attention.

/Serge.P

