I have seen this question come up again and again and again and again

Adaptec SCSI Controllers will NOT work currently in the SRM console on an
Alpha
They WILL work if you load Linux using ALphaBIOS and MILO - if you REALLY
have to.

Simply, the cards to use are:

1) Qlogic QLA1020a 20MB/S - Old product no longer available new $119
2) Qlogic QLA1040b 40MB/S - Current still the main accepted card for Alpha
SCSI $239
3) Symbios SYM53C895 Chipset based Card - 80MB/Sec $260
4) Symbios/MLSI/NCR 53C810/53C825/53C785 Narrow controller for Tape and
CDROM $79 (53C810)

Also - if it doesn't have any of the above chipsets as above on your card -
don't even bother to install it... it more than likely will not work

These are the cards we use and support (if we sell it to you)
If you want information about these cards to purchase from us we will be
glad to get information to you


