The problem is that SRM does not support Adaptec SCSI controllers, it 
will support other SCSI controllers but you can not boot to a SCSI drive 
that is connected to an Adaptec controller.  You have to use AlphaBIOS 
if you want to keep your Adaptec controller.  If you switch over to an 
IDE drive I don't see that you would have any trouble at all.  I would 
try that, but my new video card won't arrive until Tuesday.  :-(  I 
don't know why you are having trouble with it, but I would guess that 
the size has something to do with it.  Have you tried the Compaq 
Jumpstart CD?  It will create all the partitions for you.

Island computers has the right SCSI controllers (Qlogic or Symbios) but 
they are very expensive.  As an example, they charge as much for the 2MB 
Matrox Millennium II as I paid for the 8MB one. 

Good luck, let me know how it turns out.

Stephen
