On Sat, 21 Apr 2001 00:12:21 -0700, "Zufar Mulyukov" <zufar@ucsd.edu>
wrote:

>> So, does PWS have both SRM and AlphaBIOS(or ARC) ?

Yes it does. However you need a SCSI controller supported by SRM;
which the Adaptec 2940UW that is included with the PWS 433/500etc.. A
series is NOT. On the AU line they  include a Qlogic 1040B based card,
I believe the DEC part number is KZPBA. 
I also recall that my friend seems to be using a Symbios Logic/LSI
Logic card based on the 875 line that works fine. Except for spitting
out errors in installing Tru64 - though I doubt linux will give much a
damn.

On a side note with SRM, make certain you have the latest firmware so
you may use whatever sort of video card you would like, except for
NVIDIA based ones (pci tnt/tnt2's did not work whenever I tried) Older
versions only tended to like only a few particular cards like the
Matrox Millenium & the Powerstorms. Linux will not support the
Accelgraphics card that shipped with most of the  A series.

~chris


