MICHELIN Patrick <patrick.michelin@telepost.fr> writes:

>I installed RH7.0 on an Alpha LX164.
>It work fine BUT I need to hold big files on this computer.

>I have 9Go disks and want to share rhem with HP 9000 computers.
>the HP computers share that files without any problem.
>If the file in lower than 2000Mb there no problem but when bigger I
>can't do
>any command like cat, head or tail on ASCII text files nor cp, mv via
>nfs.

RH 7.0 only supports NFS V2, which only supports 32 bit file offsets.
Since lseek() handles negative offsets, only 31 bits are available,
and that means 2 GB.  NFS V3 is available in newer releases of Linux,
but is not yet available in RedHat's distribution.

While I work with NFS on Tru64 Unix, I haven't had the time or need yet
for NFS V3 on linux, so I don't have info at my finger tips.

Despite subscribing to this newsgroup, many people would say I'm woefully
ignorant of Linux issues.  For example - I don't know if Linux on Alpha
supports > 2 GB files via lseek or via the LFS (Large File Summit) API.

	-Ric Werme
