Don't you have a bootable CD?

If you do, at the P00>> prompt, enter

boot dka600 -flags 0,a0

I am assuming that 600 is your CD drive's ID, to be sure, type show dev at
the P00>> prompt. DKA0 is your boot drive, DVA0 is your floppy, and DKA600 is
usually CD. That's DEC standard configs on a AS2100.

Happy Computing!

