> Kernel panic: vfs: unable to mount root fs on 01:00
> 
> Then it stops.
> 
> Any help you can give me in this will be very much appreciated.

You shouldn't have an active UFS partition on your system; it would
seem as though the system thinks that it could boot off a UFS
filesystem, which is almost certainly the wrong answer.

One thing you're going to have to do is to provide a bit better
description of what _Linux_ CDs you're trying to use, perhaps
including how you constructed them.  I'd speculate that they are
flawed (which might be easily remedied), which prevents successful
booting.
