>player installed - but I haven't been able to get it to work within Web
>pages. How does one install the real player plugin (does it work with 4.76
>version of netscape?)

From what has already been said in this group I understand that the
problem with plug-in results from the netscape being built in different
format (ECOFF, it is a Tru64 Unix binary that Linux is able to run in a
kind of "compatibility mode"). Netscape requires its plugins be also in
ECOFF format and Real Player is in Linux' native ELF format.

So it won't work unless somebody succeeds in building Alpha/ELF
Netscape. BTW, anybody out there knowing why it's not been done?
AFAIK Netscape sources are available. Are there any serious problems in
building in under Linux/Alpha?

