I'm not sure if it's off topic here (is a compaq-ups a sys.dec ? ;-)
If so, sorry, but anyway:

Most ups do have three switched outputsignals: something like
"no mains", "battery low" and "general fault". That's all you
need. Does anybody on the net have the T1000 connectors pinout ?
Hoff, can you help ?
 
>   Anyone have any ideas?  (Best would be a linux/alpha version of
> compaq's own software:  a linux version exists!)

There is the upsd in most Linux-distributions. get the upsd
installed, set up upsd.conf, make yourself a cable (you need a free
rs232 on your linuxbox), and your ups will work on Linux. upsd will
to to init, so you have to setup your inittab, too.

Hope it helps

